From b98ac7b07b8b780a976c6b791ee86b95663f68ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Siyuan Feng <sealseacat@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 23:23:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] fix(detection): inconclusive columns are UNKNOWN, never
 silently 'safe'
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When no pattern matched and the LLM was disabled, the pipeline returned
NOT_SENSITIVE (confidence 0.5) and persisted it. An empty table or a column
the patterns don't cover was permanently stamped 'not sensitive' in history
and silently reused on every later run — even after real data arrived.

Inconclusive analysis now yields Sensitivity.UNKNOWN (confidence 0.0):
- never persisted to history, so every run re-evaluates it;
- never masked (unchanged), but no longer invisible: 'scan' prints a
  'Needs review' count and hint, 'mask' lists every unclassified column;
- ScanReport grows an .unknown property for library users.

The quickstart now demonstrates the intended workflow for such columns
(skip_column_patterns for surrogate keys, an overrides file for the rest).

---
